{"ld": 1812, "paper": "HP1213", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Establish the Loans for Trade Tools Program (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-white-russell", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-babin-mark", "h-daigle-lucien", "h-faulkingham-william", "h-guerrette-timothy", "h-mcintyre-mathew", "s-stewart-harold", "h-thorne-james", "h-white-james"], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "2106 This bill, to encourage participation in the trades, does the following. 1. It establishes the Loans for Trade Tools Program, which is a program administered by the Finance Authority of Maine to provide low-interest loans to graduates of a trade program for the purchase of tools and equipment necessary for employment in a trade. Loans are limited to $20,000 and must be repaid within 10 years. If an employee maintains full-time employment, meaning at least 32 hours per week, in the trade, that employee's loan may be forgiven.\n\n2. It establishes a tax credit for employers of employees engaged in a trade for the purchase of tools or equipment needed by that employee within the first year of employment with that employer. The credit is limited to 25% of the amount of the cost of the trade tools and $5,000 per employee, is nonrefundable and may not be carried forward from year to year.\n\n3. It provides an appropriation of $1,000,000 for each year of the 2026-2027 biennium to the Finance Authority of Maine for the Loans for Trade Tools Program.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1213&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Died On Adjournment", "final_disposition": {"label": "Died On Adjournment", "date": "2026-04-29", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1812)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1213&item=1&snum=132", "